{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>YHWH will open, etc.</b> From here begins the promise of good that corresponds to the performance of the commandments, to the very end. Therefore it concludes by saying <b>when you heed the commandments of YHWH your Elohim</b> — these are positive commandments. Now, these promises are intended to correspond to the fulfillment of the commandments, for through the commandments the channels of influx are opened and the supernal attributes are unified." "<b>And its saying YHWH will open</b> to you with the diminutive form (לְךָ): HaShem promises him that He will open for him — meaning, for him alone. The intention is that even though others may surround to stop it, through the merit of the righteous one the treasure of good will be opened. And the Name of Good is the sod of the River, and it is the sod of (Proverbs 10:25) ״צַדִּיק יְסוֹד עוֹלָם״. And its saying <b>et the heavens</b> is the sod of the supernal influx on high, as is known to those who know grace (לְיוֹדְעֵי חֵן)." "And its saying <b>and you shall lend to many nations, and you shall not borrow</b>: Now it is known that at the time when Israel do the will of the Place (HaMakom), the influx for the entire world comes through Israel, and the whole world is nourished from the distillate of the people of Israel; and conversely, when they do not, Israel are nourished from under the hand of the nations. Therefore it says ״and you shall lend to many nations and you shall not borrow״ from them. It was necessary to say ״and you shall not borrow״, for if not, there would be no recognizable sign of blessing, for the way of the world is that the great and the wealthy borrow one from another, and afterward the lender too goes back and borrows from him. Therefore it says <b>and you shall not borrow</b>, and in this there will be a recognizable sign for the statement ״and you shall lend״." "And its saying <b>and YHWH will make you the head, etc.</b> — meaning that Israel will be under the governance of the Head of the world, who is the Elohim of Israel, and not the tail, which is the celestial princes (שָׂרֵי מַעְלָה); and in this they will always be on the supreme level, as it says <b>and you shall be only above, and you shall not be below</b>, along the lines of what they said, may their memory be for blessing (Tanchuma, Vayetzei), on the verse (Jeremiah 30:10) ״וְאַתָּה אַל תִּירָא עַבְדִּי יַעֲקֹב״ — that Jacob saw in the ladder angels ascending and afterward descending; he thought that he too, after ascending, would descend. A verse came to teach him: ״אַל תִּירָא״ etc., and that is its saying ״וְלֹא תִהְיֶה לְמָטָּה״. The reason for <b>when you heed, etc.</b> — meaning, corresponding to positive commandments, as it concludes <b>and to do.</b> And the reason it did not say explicitly ״when you do the commandments״ is that there are many commandments that are not in a person's hand to perform; therefore it says <b>when you heed, etc., and to do</b> — meaning, you accept upon yourself to do. And the reason it says <b>to keep</b> in this promise: the verse comes to inform us that there is no promise for positive commandments unless preceded by observance of the negative commandments, for if not, זִבְחֵי רְשָׁעִים תּוֹעֵבָה, and every commandment that a transgressor performs draws upon it the Other Side (סִטְרָא אָחֳרָא) and bears no fruit. Therefore it preceded to say ״to keep״ and afterward said ״and to do״, which is the performance of the commandments upon which the good promises stated from ״וְהוֹתִירְךָ״ to the end were given."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:50.265786453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}